.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
An AnimMesh is an attachment to an \fBaiMesh\fP stores per-vertex animations for a particular frame\&. 

You may think of an \fBaiAnimMesh\fP as a \fRpatch\fP for the host mesh, which replaces only certain vertex data streams at a particular time\&. Each mesh stores n attached attached meshes (\fBaiMesh::mAnimMeshes\fP)\&. The actual relationship between the time line and anim meshes is established by \fBaiMeshAnim\fP, which references singular mesh attachments by their ID and binds them to a time offset\&. 
