.SS "unsigned int aiAnimMesh::mNumVertices"
The number of vertices in the \fBaiAnimMesh\fP, and thus the length of all the member arrays\&.
.PP
This has always the same value as the mNumVertices property in the corresponding \fBaiMesh\fP\&. It is duplicated here merely to make the length of the member arrays accessible even if the \fBaiMesh\fP is not known, e\&.g\&. from language bindings\&. 
.SS "\fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiVector3D\fP* aiAnimMesh::mTangents"
Replacement for \fBaiMesh::mTangents\fP\&. 
.SS "\fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiVector3D\fP* aiAnimMesh::mTextureCoords[\fBAI_MAX_NUMBER_OF_TEXTURECOORDS\fP]"
Replacement for \fBaiMesh::mTextureCoords\fP 
.SS "\fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiVector3D\fP* aiAnimMesh::mVertices"
Replacement for \fBaiMesh::mVertices\fP\&. If this array is non-nullptr, it \fImust\fP contain mNumVertices entries\&. The corresponding array in the host mesh must be non-nullptr as well - animation meshes may neither add or nor remove vertex components (if a replacement array is nullptr and the corresponding source array is not, the source data is taken instead) 
